-reported cumulative volume by end-2025; value is a lower bound because the source says over $250 million.","as_of":"2025-12-31","product_scope":"WINR-powered applications","chain_scope":["Arbitrum"],"method":"Transcribed lower bound from protocol history.","formula":"reported cumulative processed volume","raw_input_ids":[],"source_claim_ids":["casino:claim:winr:historical-adoption"],"quality_flags":["issuer_reported","lower_bound","turnover_not_revenue","application_scope_aggregated"]},{"observation_id":"casino:observation:winr:wallets:2025","case_id":"winr-protocol-bankroll","metric_dimension":"reported_unique_wallets","value":40000,"unit":"wallet","currency":null,"window_start":"2022","window_end":"2025-12-31","window_definition":"Issuer-reported unique-wallet lower bound by end-2025.","as_of":"2025-12-31","product_scope":"WINR-powered applications","chain_scope":["Arbitrum"],"method":"Transcribed lower bound from protocol history.","formula":"reported unique wallet count","raw_input_ids":[],"source_claim_ids":["casino:claim:winr:historical-adoption"],"quality_flags":["issuer_reported","lower_bound","wallets_not_people","sybil_not_adjusted"]}],"events":[{"event_id":"casino:event:winr:formation:2022","case_id":"winr-protocol-bankroll","event_type":"launch","event_date":"2022","date_precision":"year","amount_usd":null,"description":"WINR Protocol formed as separate onchain gambling infrastructure and moved its core shared-bankroll model to Arbitrum.","source_claim_ids":["casino:claim:winr:formation-migration"]},{"event_id":"casino:event:winr:staking-retired:2026","case_id":"winr-protocol-bankroll","event_type":"migration","event_date":"2026","date_precision":"year","amount_usd":null,"description":"The separate WINR staking model was retired in favor of bankroll liquidity-provider shares.","source_claim_ids":["casino:claim:winr:current-token-model"]}],"forensic_analysis":{"version":"forensic-analysis-v1","outcome":{"label":"successful","summary":"WINR achieved meaningful protocol-level proof of use by its own reported history and remains current in 2026 with an Arbitrum bankroll and creator stack. The success label is medium-confidence because volume and wallet figures are issuer-reported and current revenue, legal wrapper and licence evidence remain unresolved.","confidence":"medium","as_of":"2026-07-29","source_refs":["https://docs.winr.games/history","https://docs.winr.games/winr-token","https://docs.winr.games/liquidity-providers","https://www.winr.games/"]},"why":{"summary":"WINR moved from single-casino experiments to shared liquidity, simplified value capture into a bankroll LP, added explicit drawdown controls and now exposes game creation as a distribution strategy. This reduces fragmentation but concentrates economic and smart-contract risk in one bankroll.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["https://docs.winr.games/history","https://docs.winr.games/winr-token","https://docs.winr.games/liquidity-providers"]},"strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Replace a single casino with shared Arbitrum bankroll infrastructure that multiple products can use.","consequence":"Liquidity and risk controls are reusable across games, while a bankroll failure can affect the whole ecosystem.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://docs.winr.games/history"]},{"decision":"Retire separate staking and make WINR itself the wager, bankroll and liquidity asset.","consequence":"The token model becomes simpler and ties LP outcomes to gaming performance, increasing direct exposure to house variance and token liquidity.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://docs.winr.games/winr-token","https://docs.winr.games/liquidity-providers"]},{"decision":"Open game creation through an AI creator studio.","consequence":"Third-party content can expand distribution and catalog breadth, while introducing moderation, quality and regulatory complexity.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["https://www.winr.games/","https://docs.winr.games/history"]}],"counterfactual":{"summary":"Remaining a single casino likely would have constrained liquidity reuse and creator distribution. Supporting many isolated bankrolls could reduce common-failure concentration but fragment capital and user experience. The reviewed evidence does not quantify either tradeoff.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["https://docs.winr.games/history","https://docs.winr.games/liquidity-providers"]},"watch":[{"signal":"Current onchain bankroll value, net gaming revenue, drawdowns and withdrawal settlement.","implication":"These determine whether historical use has become sustainable current economics.","source_refs":["https://docs.winr.games/liquidity-providers"]},{"signal":"Creator-launched game count, repeat players and volume concentration by frontend.","implication":"Broad third-party use would validate infrastructure status beyond one reference application.","source_refs":["https://www.winr.games/","https://docs.winr.games/history"]}],"unknowns":["What legal entity and licences govern each consumer frontend?","What are current audited volume, revenue, TVL and unique-user figures?","How concentrated are bankroll LP shares and gameplay volume?","What oracle, contract and emergency-governance powers remain centralized?"],"review":{"status":"current","last_reviewed_at":"2026-07-29","next_review_at":"2026-08-05","reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk"}},"synthesis":{"present_situation":"WINR is active as an Arbitrum shared-bankroll and creator infrastructure system with a unified WINR asset model.","business_mechanism":"Games settle against shared WINR liquidity; net gaming results accrue through bankroll share value rather than a separate staking reward.","token_contribution":"WINR unifies wager chip, bankroll denomination and liquidity asset, increasing coherence and concentration.","chain_dependence":"Arbitrum supports settlement and bankroll accounting; frontends and some service layers remain separate from the chain.","risk_legal_posture":"Smart-contract, oracle, bankroll-variance, token-liquidity and frontend licensing risks remain material.","success_failure_hypotheses":"Shared liquidity and simplified token value flow supported proof of use; creator distribution is the next unproven growth leg.","counterfactual":"A single-app model would be simpler but less reusable; fragmented bankrolls would reduce shared-failure risk but dilute capital.","outlook":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","product_status":"active","strategy":"creator expansion","scope_guard":"Medium-confidence protocol success based partly on issuer-reported adoption."},"lessons_learned":["A shared bankroll can turn one casino into reusable infrastructure.","Wallet and volume figures need independent reconstruction before financial aggregation."],"source_claim_ids":["casino:claim:winr:formation-migration","casino:claim:winr:historical-adoption","casino:claim:winr:current-token-model","casino:claim:winr:bankroll-risk","casino:claim:winr:creator-current"],"analyst_id":"chaindump-research-desk","reviewed_at":"2026-07-29"}},{"case":{"case_id":"betswirl-onchain-casino","brand_name":"BetSwirl","entity_kind":"onchain_casino","product_subtype":"casino","legal_operator":null,"parent_entity":null,"primary_domain":"betswirl.com","launched":null,"date_precision":"unknown","custody_model":"noncustodial","chains":["Ethereum","Polygon","BNB Smart Chain","Avalanche","Arbitrum","Base","Unichain"],"product_scope_note":"This case covers BetSwirl''s noncustodial casino, PvP games, BETS token and documented contracts at betswirl.com. Token deployments include Ethereum and Unichain, while documented bank and casino-game contracts cover Polygon, BNB Smart Chain, Avalanche, Arbitrum and Base. It excludes Azuro-integrated sportsbook economics and does not treat open contracts or an audit as a gambling licence.","status":"active","status_as_of":"2026-07-29","outcome_label":"successful","outcome_as_of":"2026-07-29","outcome_rule_id":"casino-wave6-independent-onchain-revenue-v1","token_status":"documented","token_symbol":"BETS","token_name":"BETS","token_contracts":[{"chain":"EVM multichain","address":"0x94025780a1aB58868D9B2dBBB775f44b32e8E6e5","contract_role":"native token at deterministic cross-chain address"}],"token_launch_date":null,"token_utility":"BETS can be wagered in casino and PvP games, used cross-chain and paired/staked for documented reward programs.","token_fee_revenue_rights":"DefiLlama methodology attributes part of house-edge fees to dividends/holder revenue; official docs describe staking rewards and deflation. These are variable protocol mechanics, not guaranteed returns.","token_supply":{},"cohort_id":"web3-casino-wave6-2026-07-29","cohort_role":"case","selection_rule_id":"casino-wave6-product-model-contrast-v1","selection_as_of":"2026-07-29","confidence":"high","completeness_pct":93,"quality_passed":1,"human_review_required":0,"unsourced_fields":["legal_entity","gaming_licence","audited_unique_players","token_launch_date","contract_upgrade_control","jurisdiction_by_jurisdiction_availability"],"last_reviewed":"2026-07-29","updated_at":"2026-07-29"},"sources":[{"source_id":"casino:source:betswirl:contracts-2025","canonical_url":"https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/contracts","title":"Smart Contracts","publisher":"BetSwirl","published_at":"2025-11-07","accessed_at":"2026-07-29","source_tier":"B","source_role":"primary","resolving":1,"evidence_reviewed":1,"evidence_reviewed_at":"2026-07-29","evidence_reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk","notes":"Canonical deployment, audit and VRF documentation; deployment does not itself prove current demand."},{"source_id":"casino:source:betswirl:bets-2025","canonical_url":"https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/bets","title":"BETS Token","publisher":"BetSwirl","published_at":"2025-11-07","accessed_at":"2026-07-29","source_tier":"B","source_role":"primary","resolving":1,"evidence_reviewed":1,"evidence_reviewed_at":"2026-07-29","evidence_reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk","notes":"Official token address and utility source; promotional scarcity language is not treated as a price claim."},{"source_id":"casino:source:betswirl:defillama-2026-07-29","canonical_url":"https://defillama.com/protocol/betswirl?treasury=true&tvl=false","title":"BetSwirl","publisher":"DefiLlama","accessed_at":"2026-07-29","source_tier":"C","source_role":"independent","resolving":1,"evidence_reviewed":1,"evidence_reviewed_at":"2026-07-29","evidence_reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk","notes":"Independent onchain-derived metric surface with published fee/revenue methodology; figures are point-in-time and methodology-sensitive."}],"claims":[{"claim_id":"casino:claim:betswirl:deployments","case_id":"betswirl-onchain-casino","field_path":"chains.contracts.status","source_id":"casino:source:betswirl:contracts-2025","evidence_locator":"Current docs link BETS, bank, casino, PvP, multisig and Chainlink VRF contracts across named EVM networks; staking contracts are explicitly marked inactive.","claim_type":"chain","support_direction":"supports","analyst_note":"Chain list distinguishes token-only and game-contract deployments.","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"claim_id":"casino:claim:betswirl:token","case_id":"betswirl-onchain-casino","field_path":"token.contract_utility","source_id":"casino:source:betswirl:bets-2025","evidence_locator":"Docs identify identical cross-chain BETS address 0x94025780a1aB58868D9B2dBBB775f44b32e8E6e5 and wagering, PvP, staking and cross-chain uses.","claim_type":"token","support_direction":"supports","analyst_note":"No investment-value inference is made from described deflation.","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"claim_id":"casino:claim:betswirl:current-metrics","case_id":"betswirl-onchain-casino","field_path":"metrics.current_tvl_fees_revenue","source_id":"casino:source:betswirl:defillama-2026-07-29","evidence_locator":"DefiLlama snapshot reports $57,994 TVL, $25,635 fees and $12,787 revenue over 30 days, plus $869,520 cumulative revenue.","claim_type":"metric","support_direction":"supports","analyst_note":"Point-in-time onchain-derived figures; categories follow DefiLlama methodology and may be revised.","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"claim_id":"casino:claim:betswirl:fee-method","case_id":"betswirl-onchain-casino","field_path":"business.fee_allocation","source_id":"casino:source:betswirl:defillama-2026-07-29","evidence_locator":"Methodology defines fees as house edge and revenue as dividend, treasury and team allocations, with holder revenue equal to dividends.","claim_type":"metric","support_direction":"supports","analyst_note":"Methodological classification, not an audit or legal right.","checked_at":"2026-07-29"}],"licences":[],"observations":[{"observation_id":"casino:observation:betswirl:revenue-30d:2026-07-29","case_id":"betswirl-onchain-casino","metric_dimension":"protocol_revenue","value":12787,"unit":"usd","currency":"USD","window_start":"2026-06-30","window_end":"2026-07-29","window_definition":"Trailing 30-day DefiLlama protocol revenue snapshot.","as_of":"2026-07-29","product_scope":"BetSwirl onchain protocol","chain_scope":["Polygon","BNB Smart Chain","Avalanche","Arbitrum","Base"],"method":"Transcribed from DefiLlama current key metrics.","formula":"dividends + treasury + team fee allocations under DefiLlama methodology","raw_input_ids":[],"source_claim_ids":["casino:claim:betswirl:current-metrics","casino:claim:betswirl:fee-method"],"quality_flags":["third_party_methodology","point_in_time","methodology_revision_risk"]},{"observation_id":"casino:observation:betswirl:tvl:2026-07-29","case_id":"betswirl-onchain-casino","metric_dimension":"total_value_locked","value":57994,"unit":"usd","currency":"USD","window_start":null,"window_end":"2026-07-29","window_definition":"Point-in-time DefiLlama TVL snapshot.","as_of":"2026-07-29","product_scope":"BetSwirl tracked staking and pool positions","chain_scope":["Ethereum"],"method":"Transcribed from DefiLlama current key metrics.","formula":"DefiLlama TVL adapter output","raw_input_ids":[],"source_claim_ids":["casino:claim:betswirl:current-metrics"],"quality_flags":["third_party_methodology","point_in_time","not_bankroll","token_price_sensitive"]}],"events":[],"forensic_analysis":{"version":"forensic-analysis-v1","outcome":{"label":"successful","summary":"BetSwirl is a successful niche onchain casino protocol: canonical contracts span multiple EVM chains and independent methodology records current trailing-30-day revenue and cumulative revenue. Scale remains small and legal-entity and licence posture are unresolved.","confidence":"high","as_of":"2026-07-29","source_refs":["https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/contracts","https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/bets","https://defillama.com/protocol/betswirl?treasury=true&tvl=false"]},"why":{"summary":"Reusable audited contracts, Chainlink VRF, cross-chain deployment and a fee split that reaches treasury, team and token holders created a transparent product loop. The modest TVL and unresolved legal wrapper constrain scale and regulatory confidence.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/contracts","https://defillama.com/protocol/betswirl?treasury=true&tvl=false"]},"strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Deploy the same core casino and bank contracts across five EVM game networks.","consequence":"The protocol reaches multiple communities with consistent interfaces, while multiplying deployment, liquidity and monitoring complexity.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/contracts"]},{"decision":"Use Chainlink VRF and publish explorer links, audits and subgraphs.","consequence":"Results and activity are more independently inspectable than a custodial black box, although frontend and governance dependencies remain.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/contracts"]},{"decision":"Integrate BETS into wagering, PvP and holder-dividend mechanics.","consequence":"The token has product and fee utility, while demand depends on gambling volume and token liquidity.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/bets","https://defillama.com/protocol/betswirl?treasury=true&tvl=false"]}],"counterfactual":{"summary":"A single-chain launch would reduce maintenance and liquidity fragmentation but limit reach. A token without wagering or fee utility would simplify the product but weaken the current holder-alignment loop. The net effects are not measured.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/contracts","https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/bets"]},"watch":[{"signal":"Trailing fees, revenue, holder revenue, TVL and per-chain game activity.","implication":"Sustained or growing independent metrics would confirm durability; concentration or decline would weaken the result.","source_refs":["https://defillama.com/protocol/betswirl?treasury=true&tvl=false"]},{"signal":"Contract upgrades, inactive staking migrations, audits and supported-chain changes.","implication":"These can change security, token utility and operational breadth.","source_refs":["https://docs.betswirl.com/protocol-hub/protocol/contracts"]}],"unknowns":["What legal entity and licences govern the interface and protocol?","How many unique humans generate the recorded fees?","Who controls upgrades, emergency powers and treasury multisigs?","How concentrated are revenue and wagers by chain, token and user?"],"review":{"status":"current","last_reviewed_at":"2026-07-29","next_review_at":"2026-08-05","reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk"}},"synthesis":{"present_situation":"BetSwirl remains active across multiple EVM networks with current contracts, token utility and independently tracked revenue.","business_mechanism":"House-edge fees are allocated among bankroll/partners, affiliates, dividends, treasury and team under the tracked methodology.","token_contribution":"BETS supports wagers, PvP, cross-chain use and holder-alignment mechanics at a canonical multichain address.","chain_dependence":"Games, VRF, bankroll contracts, token transfers and fee accounting are materially onchain; chain fragmentation remains a cost.","risk_legal_posture":"Open contracts and audits improve technical transparency but do not establish legal operator, licence or local availability.","success_failure_hypotheses":"Composable contracts and transparent fee flow support durable niche activity; limited scale and legal opacity cap the result.","counterfactual":"Single-chain focus reduces complexity but reach; removing BETS simplifies the system but weakens its product-token loop.","outlook":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","product_status":"active","metrics_status":"current independent snapshot","scope_guard":"Niche protocol success, not universal legality or investment success."},"lessons_learned":["Independent onchain fee metrics materially strengthen a casino outcome assessment.","Audited contracts are not a substitute for operator and licence evidence."],"source_claim_ids":["casino:claim:betswirl:deployments","casino:claim:betswirl:token","casino:claim:betswirl:current-metrics","casino:claim:betswirl:fee-method"],"analyst_id":"chaindump-research-desk","reviewed_at":"2026-07-29"}}]}');
